      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The justification will pivot on defining \"meaningful agency\" not as outcome parity, but as *optimization complexity*. We will assert that the 85% dominance is the predictable result of players successfully mastering the system's highest-leverage mechanics, which requires extreme strategic depth to even reach that threshold. Therefore, the dominance isn't a replacement for strategy; it is the *reward* for achieving peak strategic execution within the designed parameters. This positions the high win rate as the ultimate validation of the game's strategic ceiling, not its lack of depth.",
      "source": "target",
